    "network": [
        {
            "tags": [
                "*"
            ],
            "prose": "Not an appetite: a ceiling. Service.Network is authorized by intersection with every ancestor -- filter_networks_with_ancestors ANDs the requested tags against the direct father's spec, then its father's, up the chain -- so a child can never reach a domain its parent did not also declare. The browser child this service launches declares '*', and '*' is matched literally by tag, so this instance has to declare it too or the child is launched with no egress at all. Worth knowing how that fails: the launch SUCCEEDS. filter_networks_with_ancestors returns an empty list, build_network_resolution raises nothing, and the guest boots with the default block_all and not one allow rule -- a browser that loads no page and reports no error. This service itself opens no outbound connection: it speaks to its node's gateway and to the child it launched. But that is a property of its code, which you can read, and not of this line, which cannot express it. See NODE-REQUIREMENTS.md #3."
        }
    ],
